    "abstract": "This study quantifies the impact of heat stress events on Brown Pelican (Pelecanus occidentalis) nesting phenology and fledging success across the Gulf of Mexico. Using temperature loggers at 12 colonies and nest monitoring data from 2018-2022 (n=387 nests), we demonstrate that extreme heat days (>37°C beach surface temperature) correlate with significantly reduced clutch sizes (p<0\.001) and increased chick mortality (p=0\.003). Sea surface warming anomalies further predicted earlier abandonment of nesting sites. Our findings highlight climate vulnerability in this coastal piscivore beyond predicted SLR impacts."
}

{
    "abstract": "We investigated hematophagous ectoparasite prevalence during prebasic molt in Semipalmated Plovers (Charadrius semipalmatus; n=73) migrating through coastal Saskatchewan (51°N, 106°W), July-September 2019. Radio-telemetry revealed high site fidelity to saline mudflats (mean residency=27.3±4.1 days). Blood smears showed 61.6\% (45/73) infected with Haemoproteus sp., with parasite load 14.3±3.1 parasites/10,000 erythrocytes. Infected individuals delayed molt initiation by 6.2±1.8 days vs. uninfected (p=0.021). This suggests parasitism may impose phenological costs affecting subsequent migration stages."
}
